{
  "about": "Building blockouts per POI and cabin area (phase 8b). Simple shapes, no detail. 'at' is [east, north] in m from the area's center in map_layout.json (so moving a POI there moves its buildings), or from the building's center for pieces 'inside' it; 'rot' is degrees clockwise from north. A building's walls are S (its front), N, E and W; an opening's 'at' is its middle, in m east or north of the wall's middle; 'floor' 0 is the ground floor. Doors and windows take their sizes from map_layout.json unless an opening gives 'width' and 'height'; an 'open' opening has no door leaf (gates). Power doors stay shut while their POI has no power. Piece types: building, block (size [width, depth, height]), cylinder, tower (cooling tower), dish, rails, train, catwalk, vehicle (mech, tank, truck), light, camera, turret, hum, underground; or 'template' with a template's name (a one-piece template takes the reference's fields; its doors, windows and inside are added to). Edit this file, then Brownout > Setup > Build Brownout Map > Buildings.",
